{
 "what": "Every byte Swell renders or computes from, pinned. The build (apps/swell/build.js) re-hashes each file and refuses on any drift; the reader's tab re-hashes the island textures it fetches. frontier-apps has no git: its files are pinned by sha256 as of the lift (2026-10-08) and named by path.",
 "lifted": "2026-10-08 from ~/Projects/frontier-apps (read only)",
 "licences": {
  "island/*.png, beaches.json (depths, K, probes)": "derived from DHN nautical chart 1902 (Marinha do Brasil, 1:100 000) + its soundings, GMRT outside the chart: NON-COMMERCIAL, NOT FOR NAVIGATION — LICENSE-DHN.md",
  "tiles/floripa.pmtiles": "© OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), tiles by Protomaps — extract of build.protomaps.com 2026-10-05, bbox -48.75,-27.95,-48.25,-27.25, z<=15 (go-pmtiles v1.31.2)",
  "pois.json": "© OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), Overpass snapshot 2026-10-05; may be incomplete",
  "code (everything else in apps/swell)": "MIT"
 },
 "sources": {
  "island model cases": "frontier-apps experiments/swell/island/cases/K-<dir>-<T>.npz (64 files, 945 MB, not lifted) and depth.npz — their sha256 are in beaches.json sources.sha256; rebuilt by frontier island.py in ~13 min (sim/island.py here is the same solver, with its battery)",
  "beaches.json": "apps/swell/sim/probes.py over those cases (2026-10-08): reproduces frontier site/swell/data/island-beaches.json probe for probe, K for all 64 cases, seaward and fetch at all 33 beaches with probes, plus the two deeper probe targets"
 },
